<body>
<main>
  <img src="lyra.png" width="280" height="85" alt="Project Lyra">
  <p class="ver">__VERSION__ &middot; Zune HD firmware 4.5</p>

  <h1>This address installs Project Lyra onto a Zune HD, from the Zune's own browser.</h1>
  <p>You are reading this on an ordinary browser, so there is nothing here for you to run.</p>

  <h2>To install</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Put the Zune HD on Wi-Fi.</li>
    <li>Open its browser and go to <code>install.zune.moe</code>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Install</strong> and leave it alone until it restarts itself.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What Lyra is</h2>
  <p>A persistent jailbreak and modding platform for the Zune HD. It adds a Mods tab to the home screen and a
  repository the device installs mods from over Wi-Fi, and it survives reboots. Nothing
  you already have on the device is touched, and it can be removed from the Mods tab.</p>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>Installing Lyra changes how the device behaves and allows arbitrary third party code
  to run. While Lyra has measures to disable mods which prevent successful booting, there
  is always a chance that the device may be unable to start and require restoring to a
  fresh state, losing your existing data. You do this at your own risk.</p>

  <footer>
    <a href="https://wiki.zune.moe/getting-started/install/">Install guide</a>
    <a href="https://wiki.zune.moe/">Wiki</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/project-lyra-zune/project-lyra">Source</a>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
